data.traces#Traces:
A tracing block exports OpenTelemetry traces over OTLP/HTTP or gRPC. The W3C traceparent of the upstream span is sent to vLLM, so vLLM’s own spans join the trace. A client’s trace context is restarted unless trust_client_context = true. Spans carry metadata only (organisation, team, key id, model, pool, priority, status, token counts, guardrail verdicts), never a prompt or an answer.
This block, with the fallbacks and audio settings above, passes llmflow-gateway check-config v0.8.0 (with the key files present, and organisations, pools and models around it):
limits { max_audio_bytes = 26214400 } tracing { endpoint = "https://otel.example.org:4318" protocol = "http" sample_ratio = 0.1 token_file = "/etc/llmflow/otel.token" insecure = false trust_client_context = false } model "whisper" { upstream_model = "openai/whisper-large-v3" pool = "small" class = "interactive" key_file = "/etc/llmflow/vllm.key" cost { audio_per_hour = 0.05 } upstream "gpu06" { base_url = "http://gpu06.internal:8000" } }
